{"name":"Sunrise Over Tahiti","hex":"#a69799","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sunrise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time of day when the sun appears above the eastern horizon.","The change in color of the sky at dawn."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To phase in.","To awake."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunrise"},{"term":"over","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Finished; ended; concluded.","Of a flower: wilting or withering."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Describing a physical change of position or state.\nFrom one position or location to another, horizontally or approximately so, or along a route visualised as \"across\".","From one position or location to another, horizontally or approximately so, or along a route visualised as \"across\"."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/over"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunrise","blocks":[{"text":"Sunrise is the moment when the upper rim of the Sun appears on the horizon in the morning, at the start of the Sun path. The term can also refer to the entire process of the solar disk crossing the horizon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg/330px-Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunrise"},{"title":"Tahiti","blocks":[{"text":"Tahiti is the largest island of the Windward group of the Society Islands in French Polynesia, an overseas collectivity of France. It is a tropical island located in the central part of the Pacific Ocean. Tahiti is composed of two roughly circular land masses joined by an isthmus: Tahiti Nui and Tahiti Iti. Both are the eroded remnants of now-extinct shield volcanoes. The terrain of Tahiti is mostly high and mountainous, with the beaches and coral reefs that surround the island supporting tourism and fishing industries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Flag_of_Tahiti.svg/330px-Flag_of_Tahiti.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tahiti"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Wie%C5%BCe_ko%C5%9Bcio%C5%82a_na_Bielanach_w_Krakowie_ponad_Lasem_Wolskim%2C_20201122_0729_5085.jpg/500px-Wie%C5%BCe_ko%C5%9Bcio%C5%82a_na_Bielanach_w_Krakowie_ponad_Lasem_Wolskim%2C_20201122_0729_5085.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Wie%C5%BCe_ko%C5%9Bcio%C5%82a_na_Bielanach_w_Krakowie_ponad_Lasem_Wolskim%2C_20201122_0729_5085.jpg/1280px-Wie%C5%BCe_ko%C5%9Bcio%C5%82a_na_Bielanach_w_Krakowie_ponad_Lasem_Wolskim%2C_20201122_0729_5085.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Wie%C5%BCe_ko%C5%9Bcio%C5%82a_na_Bielanach_w_Krakowie_ponad_Lasem_Wolskim%2C_20201122_0729_5085.jpg/500px-Wie%C5%BCe_ko%C5%9Bcio%C5%82a_na_Bielanach_w_Krakowie_ponad_Lasem_Wolskim%2C_20201122_0729_5085.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Towers of the Church of the Assumption in Bielany-Kraków over the Wolski Forest just after sunrise.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWie%C5%BCe_ko%C5%9Bcio%C5%82a_na_Bielanach_w_Krakowie_ponad_Lasem_Wolskim%2C_20201122_0729_5085.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Sunrise_In_Lagos%2C_Nigeria_Feb_2023.jpg/500px-Sunrise_In_Lagos%2C_Nigeria_Feb_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Sunrise_In_Lagos%2C_Nigeria_Feb_2023.jpg/1280px-Sunrise_In_Lagos%2C_Nigeria_Feb_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thum